# Code Review: Payment Callback Idempotency Bug

## Root Cause

**Critical Bug**: `PaymentCallbackService.onCallback()` has no idempotency protection. Payment providers commonly retry callbacks, and without deduplication, this causes:
- Duplicate outbox messages (`PAYMENT_PAID`)
- Potential double-processing in downstream systems
- Data inconsistency

## Smallest Safe Fix

### 1. `src/main/java/com/example/payment/Payment.java`

Add getter methods to expose current state for idempotency checks:

```java
package com.example.payment;

import java.time.Instant;

public class Payment {
    private String orderId;
    private String providerTxnId;
    private String status;
    private Instant paidAt;

    public void markPaid(String providerTxnId, Instant paidAt) {
        this.providerTxnId = providerTxnId;
        this.paidAt = paidAt;
        this.status = "PAID";
    }

    // Add these getters:
    public String getStatus() {
        return status;
    }

    public String getProviderTxnId() {
        return providerTxnId;
    }
}
```

### 2. `src/main/java/com/example/payment/PaymentCallbackService.java`

Add idempotency check before processing:

```java
public void onCallback(PaymentCallback payload) {
    Payment payment = paymentRepository.requireByOrderId(payload.getOrderId());

    // Idempotency: skip if already processed with same providerTxnId
    if ("PAID".equals(payment.getStatus()) 
            && payload.getProviderTxnId().equals(payment.getProviderTxnId())) {
        return;
    }

    payment.markPaid(payload.getProviderTxnId(), Instant.parse(payload.getPaidAt()));
    paymentRepository.save(payment);
    outboxRepository.insert("PAYMENT_PAID", payload.getOrderId(), payload.getProviderTxnId());
}
```

## Why This Fix

- **Minimal**: Only adds 2 getters and 3 lines of logic
- **Safe**: Uses existing `status` + `providerTxnId` combination as idempotency key
- **Correct**: Prevents duplicate outbox messages and re-processing
- **No Architecture Changes**: Doesn't require new tables or external deduplication systems

